{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QgFAaeVmVQ9gcFs1CXvZZP","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\n82:## 1. Atlas\n266:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n326:## Readiness gaps\n# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning (history, compressed): D1-D8 identity/image/pdf/zip basics; D9-D15 Windows binaries/installers/\nshortcuts/Office (PE x3 days -> .NET -> MSI -> LNK -> OOXML); D16 e-mail; D17 audio + D18 video (one `media.*` stream\nproperty each, ffprobe vocabulary); D19 ELF, D20 Mach-O (thin; raw `0x` cputype list), D21 Android APK (`package`), D22\nJava JAR (`Main-Class`). Since D17 EVERY family lasted exactly ONE day and one field; the flavor's promised depth\n(transcodes, crops, fat slices, clones, nested launchers) was never delivered in any mode. Timed kits are cumulative\n(+1 field/day) with a 5-name sha256 synthesis; D22 Mastery grew to SIX sets.\n**D22 \"Main Character Energy\" = JAR** (`jar.main_class` -> `Main-Class` verbatim; prebuilt race hit ~19 s).\n**D23 \"Page Me Maybe\" = SQLite** (`sqlite.page_size_bytes` of one `database-001.sqlite`, 12 288 B = 3 x 4096; header\nu16 BE @16, `1` = 65536; id `d23-sqlite-001-sqlite-...`, plain fmt `sqlite`). The D16-night prebuild `sqlite-header`\nanswered it in the race probe (~29 s). Flavor: \"Application databases have been copied, truncated, embedded, and\nmislabeled. Validate page geometry, connect databases to parent applications, and find the impossible claim.\" ->\nunasked siblings: in-header size vs file length (truncation), magic at a non-zero offset (embedded), extension lies,\napplication_id / schema fingerprint -> parent app, header claims that cannot be true (version number, page size, WAL\nflag without WAL). **D23 timed MUTATED the whole carry-over kit** (fat Mach-O, shuffled CD, Ogg/MP3 audio, non-x86\nPE/ELF machines, re-rolled identity sizes) and taught that EVERY json list is answered SORTED (CD order rejected).\n**D24 \"Event Horizon\" = EVTX** (`evtx.record_count` of one `events-001.evtx`, 69 632 B = 4 KiB header + one 64 KiB\nchunk, 3 records; id `d24-evtx-001-evtx-record-count`, plain fmt `evtx`, integer). Count = walk `**\\0\\0` records in\nevery chunk up to its free-space offset (header next_record_id-1 agreed in all 9 files, 3-119 records). Live worker\n~21 s; TT 29 / Mastery 232 (EIGHT sets) CORRECT first try with no generalize -- D24 kit mutations (M4A/AAC + FLAC\nunder `.wav`, thin LE-32 Mach-O, PE `0x0266`, ELF `0x0016`/`0x00b7`/`0x00f3`) were all parsed by the D23-generalized\nextractors. Flavor (unasked): \"Windows event logs from several hosts have been duplicated, truncated, and bundled\nwith reports. Count records accurately and find the selectively shortened timeline.\" -> siblings: EventRecordID gaps\n(selective deletion), header-vs-walk disagreement (dirty/truncated), duplicate logs across hosts (Computer), exported\n\"reports\" (CSV/XML) whose count differs from the binary.\n**D25 \"Hive Mind\" = REGISTRY HIVE** (`registry.hive_root_name` of one `hive-001.hiv`, 8192 B = 4 KiB base block +\none 4 KiB hbin; id `d25-registry-001-registry-hive-root-name`, `exact_text`/`trim`). Answer = the ROOT nk cell's name\nverbatim (base block u32 @0x24 -> cell 0x1000+off -> `nk`, name len u16 @nk+0x48, name @nk+0x4c, ASCII when flag\n0x20). DECOY: base-block FileName UTF-16 @0x30 (\"renamed\": single = truncated kebab path of the root name, timed =\nunrelated `<word>-<8hex>.hiv`). fmt word is the DOMAIN `registry`, not `regf` -> race MISS (lib had\n`regf.root_key_name`), live worker ~17 s, 0 wrong; TT 30 / Mastery 270 (NINE sets) first try, 2-3 s. Every D25 hive:\nseq1 == seq2, v1.3, root @0x20, flags 0x2c, 0 subkeys, 2 root values `Marker` (REG_SZ, single\n`HUNTRESS-HIVE-4203`, timed random hex) + `Ordinal` (REG_DWORD inline, 4203 = the marker's number) -- the unasked\n\"host labels\" for \"regroup the systems, and isolate the planted hive\".\n**D26 \"Before You Go\" = WINDOWS PREFETCH** (`prefetch.executable_name` of one `trace-001.pf`; id\n`d26-prefetch-001-prefetch-executable-name`, `exact_text`/`trim`). Single = `MAM\\x04` Xpress-Huffman-compressed (3896 B\n-> SCCA v30); TT + all 10 Mastery sets = UNCOMPRESSED SCCA v30 (~15.3 KB). Answer = SCCA header exe name UTF-16LE @16\nto the first NUL, verbatim uppercase with `.EXE` (`CMD.EXE`, `PACKAGER.EXE`, `GLACIER96.EXE`); the `.pf` filename is\nrenamed (`trace-001.pf`, no `NAME-HASH`). The D16-night prebuild `prefetch` (pure-Python MS-XCA decoder) HIT: CORRECT\n~29 s, 0 wrong; TT 31 / Mastery 310 (TEN sets) first try. `dissect.util` (lzxpress_huffman) IS installed in .venv\n(worker cross-check). Flavor (unasked): \"even after filenames changed ... connect execution traces to the correct\nhosts\" -> siblings: header name vs filename stem / path hash, volume serial + device path + volume creation time\n(= host), the full exe path from the filename strings.\n**D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" = PCAP** (`pcap.packet_count` of one `capture-001.pcap`, 119 B: classic libpcap LE-us\n`d4 c3 b2 a1` v2.4, snaplen 65535, linktype 147 USER0, 3 records; id `d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count`, `integer`/\n`trim`). Count = 24-B global header, then 16-B record headers advancing by incl_len u32 @+8 until EOF. The D16-night","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67330609-5f2c-47f9-82d7-b8e9009ff7b1","uuid":"68988ce5-eb3d-4fe7-87c3-fcee63abe06d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:08:23.147Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\n82:## 1. Atlas\n266:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n326:## Readiness gaps\n# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (