add disk row after pcap row\nrep(\"\"\"| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly |\"\"\",\"\"\"| `disk.*` / `gpt.*` / `mbr.*` / `.img` `.dd` `.raw` `.001` (`55 aa` @0x1FE; `EFI PART` @512 or @4096) | protective MBR type `ee` @0x1C2 -> GPT: entry LBA u64 @hdr+72, count u32 @+80, size u32 @+84; each entry {type GUID 16, unique 16, first LBA u64 @+32, last @+40, attrs @+48, name UTF-16LE @+56}; skip all-zero type GUID; keep TABLE order (D28 `partition_start_lba_sequence` = JSON ints). No GPT -> MBR 4x16 B @0x1BE {type @+4, start u32 @+8, count @+12}, types 05/0f/85 -> walk the EBR chain (logical start = EBR LBA + rel). `sfdisk -d f.img` / `fdisk -l f.img` / `sgdisk -p f.img` / `mmls f.img` cross-check. In-window: `lib/meta/prebuilt/vbr.py` (`gpt`/`mbr` fmts) + the D28 solver's `disk_partition_starts` |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly |\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Day 27 — Packet\" reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md"}}}
