ition-layout siblings of D28's start-LBA sequence on RAW images (fmt word collision fix)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/disk.py (or a new disk_layout.py registered under fmt disk + aliases image, raw_disk, disk_image, dd, gpt, mbr, partition_table): when no VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2 magic matches, parse the raw image -- GPT if MBR slot type 0xEE and `EFI PART` at LBA1 (probe 512 then 4096-B sectors), else MBR (4 x 16 B @0x1BE, EBR chain for 05/0f/85: logical start = EBR LBA + rel, next EBR = extended start + rel). Read entry LBA/count/size from the header (u64 @+72, u32 @+80, u32 @+84), skip zero type-GUID entries. GM-confirmed D28: partition_start_lba_sequence = JSON ints, TABLE order (compact). Siblings, all TABLE order, compact JSON: partition_end_lba_sequence / partition_last_lba_sequence (GPT last LBA inclusive; MBR start+count-1), partition_sector_count_sequence (end-start+1), partition_size_bytes_sequence (x sector size), partition_start_offset_bytes_sequence (start x sector size), partition_name_sequence (GPT UTF-16LE @+56, 72 B, to NUL), partition_type_guid_sequence (mixed-endian -> lowercase canonical), partition_unique_guid_sequence, partition_type_sequence (MBR `0x%02x`), partition_attributes_u64_hex_sequence; scalars partition_count, partition_table_type (`gpt`/`dos` as sfdisk prints `label:`), disk_guid (lowercase canonical), disk_signature_u32_hex (MBR @0x1B8), sector_size_bytes, first_usable_lba, last_usable_lba, alternate_lba / backup_header_lba, partition_entry_lba, partition_entry_count, partition_entry_size_bytes, image_size_bytes, image_sector_count, largest_partition_index (0-based table slot) / name. Also accept the field without `_sequence` (plural `s`, `_list`). Fixtures: build GPT images with 1-6 entries, an MBR+EBR image, a 4Kn GPT. Never sort -- `_sequence` = table order.\"},\n {\"id\":\"disk-carryover-variants\",\"concept\":\"disk-001.img as a CARRIED timed family: every shape D29+ kits may mutate it into\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D23-D27 showed every carried family mutates in TT/Mastery the day after it is introduced. Harden the partition walk (#180, disk-partition-fields) and keep start_lba_sequence correct for: MBR-only `dos` images (no 0xEE), extended + logical partitions (EBR chain, type 05/0f/85, loops guarded), hybrid MBR (0xEE + real entries -> GPT wins), 4096-B sector GPT (`EFI PART` @4096; LBAs stay in 4K sectors), non-contiguous used entries (empty slots between -> skip, keep table order), entries whose table order != LBA order (emit table order), entry_size 256 / entry count != 128, damaged primary header (bad CRC or zeroed LBA1) -> read the BACKUP header at the last LBA (its entry array sits before it), image truncated before the backup, GPT inside a VHD fixed footer / VMDK monolithicFlat / qcow2 (unwrap first), gzip/xz-compressed `.img.gz`. Fixture every case; one sample per shape in the prebuild gate.\"},\n {\"id\":\"disk-evidence-by-offset\",\"concept\":\"'Locate evidence by offset': earlier-family members embedded in a disk image\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D28 flavor: 'Disk images hold every previous artifact family in context ... locate evidence by offset'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/disk_carve.py, fmt disk (aliases image, evidence): scan the image for every family magic the lane has seen (PNG 89504e47, JPEG ffd8ff, %PDF-, PK0304, MZ+PE, 7f454c46, cffaedfe/cafebabe, d0cf11e0, 4c000000+CLSID, `SQLite format 3`, ElfFile, regf, SCCA@4 / MAM, pcap magics, OggS/RIFF/ftyp), preferring sector-aligned hits, and also map files through a FAT/NTFS/ext filesystem if one exists. Fields: evidence_offset_bytes / <family>_offset_bytes (decimal), evidence_lba / <family>_start_lba, evidence_partition_index (0-based table slot; also 1-based `_number`), evidence_offset_in_partition_bytes, embedded_family_sequence (families in offset order, lane fmt words `png` `pdf` `pe` ...), embedded_member_count, evidence_sha256 (carve by the format's own length: PNG IEND, zip EOCD, PE SizeOfImage/last section, SQLite page_size x page_count, EVTX chunks, regf hbins size, pcap record walk). Question may name the evidence by its old member name (`panel-001.png`) -> match by magic + family.\"},\n {\"id\":\"disk-rebuilt-integrity\",\"concept\":\"'Prove which image was rebuilt from an incomplete source': GPT/MBR consistency and truncation checks\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/disk_integrity.py, fmt disk (aliases gpt, image). Fields (enum true|false unless noted): primary_header_crc_valid (CRC32 of hdr_size bytes with @+16 zeroed), partition_array_crc_valid (CRC32 of count x size @entry LBA vs @+88), backup_header_present (`EFI PART` at the last LBA AND at alternate_lba), backup_matches_primary (same disk GUID/entries/usable range; my_lba/alternate swapped), alternate_lba_matches_image_end, image_truncated (alternate_lba or any partition last LBA >= image sector count), partitions_beyond_image_count, protective_mbr_size_matches (0xEE count = min(sectors-1, 0xFFFFFFFF)), overlapping_partitions, zero_filled_partition_sequence / empty_partition_count, header_crc32_u32_hex / partition_array_crc32_u32_hex (`0x%08x` stored and computed), integrity_status / rebuilt_indicator enum (`intact`, `rebuilt`, `truncated`, `crc_mismatch` -- unverified spelling, also emit the booleans). Multi-image synthesis: 'which image was rebuilt' = the image whose backup/CRC/size claims are inconsistent; answer its member filename.\"},\n {\"id\":\"disk-image-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-image synthesis over several disk-NNN.img members (and the D15+ digest-order synthesis carrying a large .img)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py: ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` with Files listing disk images: order by partition_count / first start LBA / image size / disk GUID, group images by identical partition layout (same start/end sequence), 'rebuilt image' = the one failing disk-rebuilt-integrity or whose layout matches another but whose partition contents are zero/truncated, partition-content sha256 per image (hash each partition's byte range: partition_sha256_sequence). D28 synthesis already hashed a multi-100-KB `.img` in-window; keep per-set byte caching (no id()-keyed caches, D25).\"},\n {\"id\":\"filesystem-in-partition-walk\",\"concept\":\"The layer inside a partition: filesystem directory walk -> file names, sizes, start cluster, byte offset\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/fs_walk.py, fmts fat (aliases fat12, fat16, fat32, vfat), exfat, ntfs, ext (aliases ext2, ext3, ext4), filesystem, disk (partition-relative: accept `partition_N_` / `pN_` prefixes, default first partition). Reuse vbr.py for the boot sector. FAT: root dir (FAT12/16 fixed region; FAT32 root cluster @0x2C), 32-B dirents + LFN (0x0F) reassembly, deleted 0xE5, cluster chain via FAT -> file_names (sorted), file_count, volume_label (dirent attr 0x08), <file>_start_cluster, <file>_offset_bytes (image-absolute = part_lba*ss + data_region + (clus-2)*cluster_size), <file>_size_bytes, created/modified times (DOS local -> `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`). exFAT: 0x85/0xC0/0xC1 entry sets, label 0x83. NTFS: $MFT at mft_cluster*cluster -> FILE records (fixups) -> $FN names, $DATA resident/non-resident first run -> offset. ext4: superblock @1024 (`53 ef` @0x38): volume_name @0x78, uuid @0x68, last_mounted @0x88, block size, inode 2 root dir (extents 0xF30A or block map) -> names. Cross-check with TSK `fls -o <lba> f.img` / `icat` / `fsstat` (installed, worker-only).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ewf-forensic-images\",\"concept\":\"Forensic acquisition containers: EWF/E01 (+Ex01, L01), split raw .001/.002, AFF4, SMART\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"'Rebuilt from an incomplete source' smells like an E01 whose stored MD5/SHA1 no longer matches the media. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/ewf.py, fmt ewf (aliases e01, expert_witness, forensic_image, image): signature `EVF\\\\x09\\\\x0d\\\\x0a\\\\xff\\\\x00` @0 (EWF2 `EVF2\\\\r\\\\n\\\\x81\\\\x00`), segment number u16 @9; sections {type 16 B, next u64, size u64, crc}: `header`/`header2` (zlib -> tab-separated text: case_number c, evidence_number n, description a, examiner_name e, notes t, acquisition date m / system date u, os, acquiry software version av, password hash p), `volume`/`disk` (chunk_count u32 @4, sectors_per_chunk @8, bytes_per_sector @12, sector_count u64 @16, media type, compression level, set GUID @64), `table`/`sectors` (chunk offsets, bit 31 = compressed), `hash` (MD5 16 B), `digest` (MD5 + SHA1), `done`. Fields: case_number, evidence_number, examiner_name, description, notes, acquisition_date, acquisition_software, media_size_bytes, sector_count, bytes_per_sector, chunk_count, stored_md5, stored_sha1, computed_md5 (inflate every chunk, zlib), hash_matches (true|false), segment_count. Split raw `.001..`: concatenate by number; `<name>.001` size sums.\"},\n {\"id\":\"linux-mac-fs-superblocks\",\"concept\":\"Non-Windows filesystem superblocks: ext2/3/4, XFS, Btrfs, HFS+, APFS container\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Module lib/meta/prebuilt/fs_super.py, fmts ext (ext2/ext3/ext4), xfs, btrfs, hfs (hfsplus), apfs, plus fmt filesystem auto-detect. ext: superblock @1024, magic 0xEF53 @0x38, inodes/blocks count @0/@4, log_block_size @0x18 (1024<<v), mtime/wtime @0x2C/@0x30 (u32 epoch), state @0x3A, rev @0x4C, feature_compat/incompat/ro_compat @0x5C/@0x60/@0x64 (-> ext2/ext3 has_journal/ext4 extents|flex_bg|64bit), uuid @0x68, volume_name @0x78 (16 B), last_mounted @0x88 (64 B), mkfs_time @0x108. XFS `XFSB` @0 BE: blocksize @4, dblocks u64 @8, uuid @32, fname @108. Btrfs `_BHRfS_M` @0x10040: fsid @0x10020, label @0x1012B. HFS+ `H+`/`HX` @0x400 BE: create/modify date (s since 1904), blockSize, totalBlocks. APFS `NXSB` @32: block size @36, block count @40, uuid @72. Fields: filesystem_type, volume_label/name, uuid, block_size_bytes, block_count, last_mounted_path, created/last_mount/last_write times ISO `Z`. Route from a disk partition start LBA as well (disk + partition index).\"},\n {\"id\":\"encrypted-volume-headers\",\"concept\":\"Encrypted volumes inside disk images: LUKS1/LUKS2, BitLocker, FileVault/CoreStorage, VeraCrypt hidden\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt luks: `LUKS\\\\xba\\\\xbe` @0, version u16 BE @6; v1: cipher_name 32 B @8, cipher_mode @40, hash_spec @72, payload_offset u32 @104, key_bytes @108, uuid 40 B @168, active key slots (8 x 48 B from @208, 0x00AC71F3 = enabled); v2: hdr_size u64 @8, label 48 B @24, checksum_alg @72, uuid @168, JSON area after 4096 B (keyslots/segments/digests -> cipher, sector size). fmt bitlocker: VBR OEM `-FVE-FS-` @3 (Vista `MSWIN4.1`), FVE metadata block GUIDs at offsets @0xA0/@0xA8/@0xB0 (u64), metadata `-FVE-FS-` sig, version u16, volume GUID, encryption method u16 (0x8000 AES-128-diffuser ... 0x8004 XTS-AES-128, 0x8005 XTS-AES-256), creation FILETIME, description UTF-16 (`<host> <drive> <date>`). VeraCrypt: no magic (entropy only) -> `none`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"lvm-raid-ldm\",\"concept\":\"Pooled / multi-disk volume metadata: LVM2, Linux md RAID, Windows LDM dynamic disks, Storage Spaces\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt lvm (aliases lvm2, pv): label `LABELONE` in one of the first 4 sectors (sector number u64 @8, crc @16, offset @20, `LVM2 001` @24), PV header uuid 32 chars @label+32, device size u64, metadata area -> text `vg_name { id = ... seqno = N ... logical_volumes { lv_name { segment1 { start_extent, extent_count, stripes = [\\\"pv0\\\", N] } } } }` -> vg_name, vg_uuid, seqno, pv_uuid (hyphenated 6-4-4-4-4-4-6), lv_names (sorted), extent_size, lv_segments. fmt mdraid: v0.90 superblock at end (64 KiB aligned) magic 0xa92b4efc, v1.x @0/@4096/@8 KiB: level, raid_disks, uuid, name, ctime. fmt ldm: MBR type 0x42 / GPT type 5808c8aa-7e8f-42e0-85d2-e1e90434cfb3, `PRIVHEAD` @ LBA 6 (or end of disk), disk GUID text, `TOCBLOCK`, `VMDB` -> volume names. Fields: is_dynamic, disk_group_name, volume_names.\"},\n]\nfor n in new: assert n['id'] not in ids, n['id']\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\n# order: notes p1, new p1, others by priority (stable)\nnotes=[g for g in gaps if g['priority']==1]\nrest=[g for g in gaps if g['priority']!=1]\np1new=[n for n in new if n['priority']==1]\nothers=sorted(rest+[n for n in new if n['priority']!=1], key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nout=notes+p1new+others\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(body)\ns=s[:js_a]+body+s[js_b:]\n# ranking paragraph\na=s.index(\"Ranking (D27 post-run)\"); b=s.index(\"TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail`\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"Ranking (D28 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D29-D31 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD28 went from network evidence down to the DISK holding everything (`disk.partition_start_lba_sequence` of a raw GPT\nimage) and the race MISSED on a fmt-word collision (lib `disk` = virtual-disk containers). Its flavor names\n\"every previous artifact family in context\", \"locate evidence by offset\" and \"prove which image was rebuilt from an\nincomplete source\", and the title reads like a finale arc, so priority 1 = the `disk` fmt on raw images with every\npartition-layout sibling, the carried disk family's timed mutations (MBR/EBR/4Kn/backup header/wrappers), evidence\ncarved by offset, image integrity, cross-image synthesis and the filesystem layer inside the partition. Forensic\nimage containers (E01), non-Windows superblocks and cloud/identity audit logs at 2; encrypted/pooled volumes and\ncerts-in-capture at 3. The built D27 pcap/network priority-1 items moved to 2 (built; the prebuild drains only\nunbuilt `prebuild` gaps).\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\npend=[g['id'] for g in out if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(out),'gaps; pending prebuild:',len(pend),pend)\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3774,"cache_read_input_tokens":123297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3774},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67330609-5f2c-47f9-82d7-b8e9009ff7b1","uuid":"c37d7b44-db15-4bc1-a117-1cef2b5012ef","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:13:49.632Z","request_id":"req_011CgUhAY8Mg4YfuWV3CnTYT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XQbs5kBA3CSoi6W73cGapY":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ng0=s.index('## Readiness gaps')\nm=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',s[g0:],re.S)\njs_a=g0+m.start(1); js_b=g0+m.end(1)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(1))\nids={g['id'] for g in gaps}\nbyid={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\n# re-rank: D27 pcap p1 items -> 2 (built)\nfor k in [\"prefetch-carryover-variants\",\"pcap-carryover-variants\",\"pcap-malformed-integrity\",\"pcap-l3l4-decode\",\"pcap-app-indicators\",\"network-flow-log-exports\",\"host-network-evidence\",\"host-vs-network-synthesis\"]:\n    byid[k]['priority']=2\nv=byid[\"ntfs-boot-sector-vbr\"]\nv[\"concept\"]=\"Filesystem/disk boot structures: NTFS $Boot VBR, FAT/exFAT VBR, MBR partition table, GPT header (GPT start LBAs SEEN D28 under fmt `disk`)\"\nv[\"detail\"]=\"BUILT as lib/meta/prebuilt/vbr.py. D28 asked `disk.partition_start_lba_sequence` (raw GPT image) -- vbr.py had the walk only under fmts gpt/mbr/partition_table as